<br>

## Filter on range of values

Suppose I want to cut down on spending and only keep streaming services with prices between $7 and $10. I can use the `is_between` expression in Polars to achieve this. Here's how to do it:

::: {#c8829ba8 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .filter(pl.col('Price').is_between(7.99,10.99))
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (4, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Subscription</th><th>Price</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Hulu&quot;</td><td>7.99</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Showtime&quot;</td><td>10.99</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Disney+&quot;</td><td>7.99</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;AMC&quot;</td><td>8.99</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


## Exclude some or both bounds

By default, `is_between` includes both the left and right bounds. You can choose to exclude either the left or right bound, or even both. Here's how to exclude the left bound:

::: {#925823b5 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .filter(pl.col('Price').is_between(7.99,10.99, closed='right'))
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (2, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Subscription</th><th>Price</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Showtime&quot;</td><td>10.99</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;AMC&quot;</td><td>8.99</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


<br>

To exclude the right bound instead, replace `'right'` with `'left'` in the `closed` parameter. Here's how you can exclude both the left and right bounds:

::: {#744316ef .cell execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .filter(pl.col('Price').is_between(7.99,10.99, closed='none'))
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}
